Z||000012||Cozmo||11-10-2001||11:39 AM||||OK, after further examination, here's what I've discovered...<BR>The guy I got it from threw in a black '88 Coupe nose and the engine grilles were in the trunk, so at least all the body panels are there now.  There is a small tear in the middle of the rear fascia, but besides that the body is in great shape, even the paint is decent.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88back.jpg"> <BR>After getting the trunk open, I found out the P.O. had disconnected everything on the top end of the engine.  Looks like he was preparing to drop the cradle (less work for me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).  Since the trunk was filled with empty bottles of "Motor Medic" and "Knock be Gone", I assume the engine is toast.  The radiator is gone, and so are the headlight assemblies, instrument cluster, radio, and exhaust.  The brakes and steering seem OK and the suspension seems tight.<BR>As far as it's future, it's going to be converted into a Cadero (Caddy 4.9 V8).<BR>I think it'll be a perfect car for that, as it has the good suspension and brakes to start with.  I'll keep the TH125 auto so it shouldn't be too difficult of a swap (yeah, right...)<BR>I couldn't pass this one up guys, it's an excellent blank canvas to make a real sleeper out of...<P>BobC  ||||reg||1
